# TEMPLATE — not applied, not encrypted, not read by anything. It exists so the
# shape of the real file is reviewable in git while the real file is opaque
# ciphertext. ./moneyman-config.sops.yaml already exists next to it with these
# same placeholders encrypted, so the operator's job is `sops` on that file
# rather than a copy — this one stays, as the diffable reference for what each
# placeholder means.
#
# Every key below was checked field by field against moneyman's own zod schema
# at the pinned release `v2026.07.18.1` (`src/config.schema.ts`), not against
# upstream's README, because the README is looser than the schema. The
# top-level object accepts exactly three keys — `accounts`, `storage`,
# `options` — and silently drops anything else, so a typo here costs a setting
# with no error anywhere.
#
# `accounts` entries are a loose object: `companyId` and `password` are typed,
# and everything else passes straight through to israeli-bank-scrapers (v6.8.0
# at this release), which is where the per-bank field names come from. Its
# `src/definitions.ts` gives hapoalim `userCode` + `password` and isracard
# `id` + `card6Digits` + `password`; `id` is the national ID number.
#
# `storage.actual` is `serverUrl` / `password` / `budgetId` / `accounts`.
# `password` is Actual's *server* password, the one set interactively on first
# visit to budget.tomkatom.com, not an Actual user account. `budgetId` is the
# Sync ID from Settings then Advanced. `accounts` maps scraper-side account id
# to Actual account UUID, and the key is specifically israeli-bank-scrapers'
# `account.accountNumber` — the UUID is the one in the account page's URL.
#
# `serverUrl` is the in-cluster Service DNS of the Actual server, verified by
# rendering ../actual.yaml's values with app-template 5.0.1: the Service is
# named `actual` on port 5006. It is deliberately not budget.tomkatom.com —
# Authelia's forwardAuth is a Traefik middleware annotation on the Ingress, so
# it gates the public hostname only, and moneyman has no way to hold a session
# anyway. The consequence is that this address is a coupling recorded in
# ciphertext where ../media-common/media-urls.yaml would record it in the
# clear: a PR that renames Actual's Service or moves its port has to carry a
# `sops` edit of the real file in the same commit, because nothing validates
# the two against each other.
#
# `options.scraping.transactionHashType: "moneyman"` is load-bearing and is
# the one value here that must be right *before the first import*. See the
# header of ./moneyman-config.sops.yaml for the full argument; the short
# version is that it is what makes `daysBack: 14` overlap free, and that
# changing it later re-imports the whole window as duplicates.
#
# `options.logging.getIpInfoUrl: false` suppresses an outbound call to
# ipinfo.io that moneyman otherwise makes on every run. It is not a security
# control, just an egress the lab has no use for; the schema accepts the
# literal `false` or a URL.
#
# `options.notifications.telegram` exists upstream (`apiKey`, `chatId`,
# `enableOtp`, `otpTimeoutSeconds`, `sendLogFileToTelegram`) and is left out on
# purpose. Alerting in this lab rides one path — Prometheus to Alertmanager to
# the Telegram group — and adding moneyman's own notifier would put the bot
# token in a third encrypted home to rotate. Note that `storage.telegram` is a
# different thing again: it ships the scraped transactions themselves to a
# chat, and is not wanted here at all.
#
# ⚠ Placeholders read `FILL_ME` rather than this repo's usual
# `<paste-something-here>` because they sit inside a JSON document, where the
# angle-bracket form reads like markup rather than like a blank. They are still
# just strings; nothing parses them.
#
# ⚠ In the real file, the value under `MONEYMAN_CONFIG` must stay a block
# scalar (`|`). A block scalar is a string, and `stringData` is
# map[string]string — retyped as a flow scalar the Secret can still encrypt and
# then fails only at Argo sync time, with every other resource in the overlay
# applied and this one Secret missing. CI greps for the `type:str` tag so that
# lands at PR time instead.
#
# ⚠ This file's name matters twice over. ../../../../.sops.yaml matches
# `clusters/.*\.sops\.ya?ml$` with `encrypted_regex: ^(data|stringData)$`, so
# only the payload of the real file is encrypted and its metadata stays
# diffable. And ./secret-generator.yaml lists `moneyman-config.sops.yaml` by
# that exact name: until the encrypted file exists at that path the ksops
# generator cannot resolve it and the whole finance-common overlay fails to
# render in the repo-server. The `.example` suffix is what keeps *this* file
# out of both CI's sops type check (`find clusters -name '*.sops.yaml'`) and
# its direct-CR kubeconform lint (`find clusters -name '*.yaml'`); neither
# pattern matches it, and yamllint skips it too.
apiVersion: v1
kind: Secret
metadata:
  name: moneyman-config
  namespace: finance
type: Opaque
stringData:
  MONEYMAN_CONFIG: |
    {
      "accounts": [
        { "companyId": "hapoalim", "userCode": "FILL_ME", "password": "FILL_ME" },
        { "companyId": "isracard", "id": "FILL_ME_TZ", "card6Digits": "FILL_ME", "password": "FILL_ME" }
      ],
      "storage": {
        "actual": {
          "serverUrl": "http://actual.finance.svc.cluster.local:5006",
          "password": "FILL_ME_ACTUAL_SERVER_PASSWORD",
          "budgetId": "FILL_ME_SYNC_ID",
          "accounts": { "FILL_ME_SCRAPED_ACCOUNT_NUMBER": "FILL_ME_ACTUAL_ACCOUNT_UUID" }
        }
      },
      "options": {
        "scraping": {
          "daysBack": 14,
          "futureMonths": 1,
          "maxParallelScrapers": 1,
          "transactionHashType": "moneyman"
        },
        "logging": { "getIpInfoUrl": false }
      }
    }
